      "math_academy_id": "q-224486",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(6)$ given below, compute $P(2<X\\le 5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0620\\,$ | $\\,0.1512\\,$ | $\\,0.2851\\,$ | $\\,0.4457\\,$ | $\\,0.6063\\,$ | $\\,0.7440\\,$ | $\\,0.8472\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(5) & =P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\})+P(X\\in \\{3,4,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 2)+P(2<X\\le 5) \\\\  & =F(2)+P(2<X\\le 5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X\\le 5) & =F(5)-F(2) \\\\  & =0.4457-0.0620 \\\\  & =0.3837.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
      "result": "Correct",
      "grade": "Correct",
